From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Telephony: Don't log every satellite config lookup

SatelliteController asks TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver for the
satellite config parser from dozens of places, and each lookup logged
"getConfigParser: domain=satellite". On a dual SIM phone that ran at
about 5 lines a second, around 300 a minute, in com.android.phone for as
long as the phone was awake. The lookup returns a cached parser; only log
when one is created.
---
 .../configupdate/TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver.java       | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/configupdate/TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/configupdate/TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver.java
index 93283ad060..c491a57a89 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/configupdate/TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/configupdate/TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver.java
@@ -597,7 +597,6 @@ public class TelephonyConfigUpdateInstallReceiver extends ConfigUpdateInstallRec
     @Nullable
     @Override
     public ConfigParser getConfigParser(String domain) {
-        Log.d(TAG, "getConfigParser: domain=" + domain);
         ConfigParser parser = getInstance().mConfigParsers.computeIfAbsent(domain, d -> {
             Log.d(TAG, "CreateNewConfigParser with domain " + d);
             ConfigParser newParser = getNewConfigParser(
-- 
